## 10. Shell Security  
Shell access is powerful and dangerous.  
Implement permission levels:  
```
SAFE
NORMAL
ELEVATED
DANGEROUS
```
Examples:  
```
ls
pwd
git status
cat file
```
→ SAFE  
```
pip install package
npm install
git checkout
```
→ NORMAL  
```
sudo ...
chmod ...
systemctl ...
```
→ ELEVATED  
```
rm -rf
disk formatting
destructive system operations
credential manipulation
```
→ DANGEROUS  
Never silently execute dangerous operations.  
Provide:  
```
Allow once
Allow for session
Deny
```
and preferably:  
```
Always allow this exact command
Always allow commands matching this safe pattern
```
Do not create a security bypass mechanism.  
   
⸻  
   
